# Personal Learning Goals

These are the things I want to achieve in CPELX230-330 (Agentic Software Engineering).

## 1. Learn how to build software from start to finish
I want to understand the whole software development life cycle (SDLC): planning, designing, coding, testing, releasing, and maintaining. My aim is to turn an idea into a working program that is organized, tested, and easy to maintain.

## 2. Learn how to properly integrate AI into my coding
I want to use AI as a helper, not a shortcut. This means writing clear prompts, then reviewing, testing, and understanding every piece of AI-generated code before I use it. I also want to learn how to build a simple AI agent and connect it to tools and APIs.

## 3. Use Git and GitHub confidently
I want to be comfortable with the basics of Git: making clear commits, pushing and pulling changes, and working with teammates so my work is easy to trace.

## 4. Work well in an Agile team
I want to learn how Scrum works, including sprints, roles, and reviews, and practice teamwork and communication on the class project.

## 5. Learn how to manage repositories properly
I want to keep my repositories clean, organized, and professional. This includes a clear folder structure, a helpful README, meaningful commit messages, and using branches and pull requests. I also want to keep passwords, API keys, and personal data out of my repositories.

## How I Will Measure My Progress
- I can explain my code and how AI helped me write it.
- My projects have tests and clear documentation.
- My repositories are well organized, with a clear README and a consistent commit history.
- I include an AI disclosure statement whenever AI helps with my work.
